==English==

{{wikipedia|Whistleblower}}

===Etymology===
Probably an [[allusion]] to a [[police officer]] blowing his or her whistle on observing a violation of the law.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[whistle]][[-]][[blower]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} One who [[report]]s a [[problem]] or [[violation]] to the [[authorities]]; especially, an [[employee]] or former employee who reports a violation by an [[employer]].''
#: ''We owe it to a small group of brave '''whistle-blowers''' that we know about the infractions at all.''

====Synonyms====
* [[Wikisaurus:informant]]

